AB  - Do neural network models capture the cognitive demands of human reasoning? Across seven reasoning tasks, we show that the length of the chain-of-thought generated by large reasoning models predicts human reaction times both within tasks—tracking item-level difficulty—and across tasks—capturing broader differences in cognitive demands. This model-to-human alignment shows that out-of-the-box reasoning models reflect core features underlying problem and task complexity in human cognition, without requiring any built-in symbolic mechanisms.
